⍝ HTTP handlers for UW Schedule Exporter.
⍝ The page itself is site/index.html, which Jarvis serves as a static file (see start).
:Namespace web

      ∇ r←req ProcessSchedule _;schedule;summary;description;dateFormat
      ⍝ HTTP POST handler: convert a pasted Quest schedule to an iCalendar file.
      ⍝ req.Payload (JSON):
      ⍝   schedule    - raw text copied from the Quest Class Schedule page
      ⍝   summary     - template for event titles (see README for @variables)
      ⍝   description - template for event descriptions
      ⍝ Returns the .ics text. If the schedule can't be read, returns a short
      ⍝ plain-text explanation with status 400 (bad input) or 500, for the page to show.
          :Trap 0
              schedule←req.Payload.schedule
              summary←req.Payload.summary
              description←req.Payload.description
              schedule dateFormat←##.uwsch schedule
              r←summary description dateFormat ##.ical schedule
              req.Response.Headers←3 2⍴'Content-Type' 'text/calendar; charset=utf-8' 'Content-Disposition' 'attachment; filename="schedule.ics"' 'Cache-Control' 'no-store'
          :Else
              ⍝ Log what failed, never the schedule itself
              ⎕←'ProcessSchedule: ',⎕DMX.(EM,(0<≢Message)/': ',Message)
              (r status)←Problem ⎕DMX.EM
              req.Response.Headers←2 2⍴'Content-Type' 'text/plain; charset=utf-8' 'Cache-Control' 'no-store'
              req.Fail status
          :EndTrap
      ∇

      Problem←{
      ⍝ Error message ⍵ from uwsch/ical → (text for the user) (HTTP status)
          ⍵≡'NO_DATES':'No class dates were found. Copy the whole Class Schedule page from Quest in List View (Ctrl+A, then Ctrl+C) and paste all of it.' 400
          ⍵≡'AMBIGUOUS':'Couldn''t tell whether the dates are day/month or month/day, because none is after the 12th of its month.' 400
          ⍵≡'INCONSISTENT Dates':'The dates mix day/month and month/day order, or include a date that doesn''t exist.' 400
          'Couldn''t read that schedule. Make sure you copied the whole Class Schedule page from Quest in List View.' 500
      }

:EndNamespace
